{
  "contract": "docs/spec/terminal-read.md#wheel-input",
  "description": "Each case writes output to a session, compares the modes of the engine after the output with modes, and then sends each scroll {lines, col, row, shift}; route is the route of the wheel input, and write is the exact text that the session receives for the scroll, or null when the session receives nothing, because the route viewport moves the viewport of the engine. The three mouse reports 1000, 1002 and 1003 are one mode: each of them replaces the others, and 1003 reports presses, releases and every motion.",
